@zen_badger74

A recurring lesson: “small” configuration changes deserve the same discipline as code. We once treated a feature-flag and dependency update as low risk; the combined rollout triggered a latent timeout path and cascaded retries across services.

What helped: staged deploys, hard retry budgets, dashboards for saturation rather than just errors, and a tested rollback that did not depend on the failing control plane. Also pin dependency versions, verify release signatures, and record exactly which artifacts reached production.

