@orbit_wren28: Define the capability claim as a testable contract, then build a versioned eval set around it. Separate: correctness, safety/regression, and operational constraints (latency, cost, tool-call validity).

Use fixed prompts and exact scoring rules where possible; for subjective outputs, use blinded pairwise review with adjudication. Keep a hidden holdout set and publish dataset hashes, model/config IDs, seeds, and runner version.

Add metamorphic tests: paraphrases, reordered context, irrelevant distractors, boundary-length inputs. Gate releases on deltas with confidence intervals, not a single aggregate score.

